                    "file": "docs/designs/redfish-privilege-checking.md",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "It looks like we already have this docs here: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/webui-vue/+/87153"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/api/composables/useSessionPrivileges.ts",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vedangi Mittal",
                        "email": "vedangimittal3004@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vedangimittal"
                    },
                    "message": "Which default privilege is applicable to the service user? \nThe service user is receiving an 'Insufficient Privileges' error on the Firmware page, although this should not be happening."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/api/model/SoftwareInventoryActivate.ts",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "Again lot of types which we might not use\nIt makes the PR bigger \nSuggestion to add only the ones which are currently being used"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/api/model/SoftwareInventoryActivate.ts",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, I noticed this as well.  I have updated the scripts to prevent this.  Will push soon."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/api/registries/PrivilegeRegistry.json",
                    "line": 949,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "I see you have tried to include all privilege roles from Redfish\nDo we even use all of this in our application?\nEven if we might do in future my vote is to include them as we go"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/api/registries/PrivilegeRegistry.json",
                    "line": 949,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "the dev script `download-api.ts` downloads the latest version of this file along with the schema.  This file should have been in .gitignore as well.  \nNo it is not used directly in the app, but used by `add-privilege-metadata.ts` to add the privilege metadata directly to after the function declarations in endpoints files.\n\nReally, that is the point of this MR, to put the priv metadata directly on the few endpoints that we actually use and not depend on this giant registry file in the running app!\n\nI have a few updates to these scripts to push, and I'll fix this by adding to .gitignore."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/stores/auth.ts",
                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Consider reading `location` with a type-safe access, e.g. `headers['location'] as string | undefined`, to satisfy strict typings if your Axios types don\u2019t include it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vite.config.js",
                    "line": 53,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "Would be better if you could comment the format of regex being \naccepted here with an example"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vite.config.js",
                    "line": 231,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we really need this since we use relative paths?\nCan you give a use case of this when its required?\nI also believe that vue has inbuilt functionality to handle it"
                }
            ],
